SCOPE: WHAT THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE COVERS

The MIT License above covers the original work of the copyright holder: the
source code in src/, scripts/, tests/ and apps/, the notebooks in notebooks/,
and the documentation in docs/. It is granted so that the method, the seeds,
the pinned environment and the workflow can be inspected, re-run and verified
by anyone, which is what a reproducible research repository requires.

THIRD PARTY DATA IS NOT COVERED

This repository includes or retrieves data from third parties, including EM-DAT
(CRED, UCLouvain), the Colombo Stock Exchange, the World Bank, NASA POWER,
DesInventar, FRED and Wikidata. Those sources carry their own terms of use and
their own citation and redistribution requirements.

The MIT License above grants NO rights over any third party data, and it does
not override, replace or relax the terms of any third party source. Anyone
redistributing or reusing the contents of data/ or artifacts/external/ must
satisfy the originating source's terms directly. Each source, its provenance
and its terms are documented in docs/data_sources.md.

In particular, the raw EM-DAT export and the Colombo Stock Exchange archive
under data/raw/ are third party material retained here for verification of the
published results. They are not licensed for redistribution by this file.

